## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical KCA design for mobile field devices in multi-region deployments, focusing on real-world constraints like unreliable networks and urgent revocation needs.

## Key Concepts
- Regional attestation and baseline image trust
- Short-lived TLS certificates with SPIFFE IDs
- Per-app policy binding and code-signing for mobile apps
- Offline revocation checks and audit logs
- Recovery tests for connectivity loss and device loss

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch: enrollment flow
function enrollDevice(device, region){
  attestToRegionalBootstrap(region);
  const cert = requestCertificateFromKCA({region, deviceId: device.id}, TTL_120s, 'techfield');
  bindAppPolicies(cert, device.appId);
  enableOffline_revocation(cert);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate keys without service disruption?
- What monitoring would you add for revocation propagation across regions?

